From c2e7caeeb4676da137b03ad82b557863635a21fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:31:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] jay: bake cross-pipe RegDist into in-order instructions
 on Xe-HP+

lower_regdist() put every dependency on a pipe other than the inferred one
into a separate SYNC.nop, which is only required on Gfx12.0 (no pipe field
in the SWSB) and for instructions that also take an SBID. Since Xe-HP the
SWSB of an in-order instruction can name the pipe (or A@n for several
pipes), which is what brw does (baked_ordered_dependency_mode).

Wuthering Waves RT shaders are bound on instruction fetch, and these
SYNC.nop were 9.1% of their code. ptbench: raygen code -7..-12%, all
shaders -4.9% bytes; I-cache bound 'huge' raygen 161.7 -> 135.5 ms,
images bit-identical. vkd3d-proton d3d12 suite and rtpipe matrix unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_lower_scoreboard.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_lower_scoreboard.c b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_lower_scoreboard.c
index ff44d299bfe..36df1c0adc5 100644
--- a/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_lower_scoreboard.c
+++ b/src/intel/compiler/jay/jay_lower_scoreboard.c
@@ -730,8 +730,14 @@ lower_regdist(jay_function *func, jay_inst *I, struct swsb_regdist_state *ctx)
 
    /* DPAS and slow ALU on Gfx12 can only represent in-order dependency for its.
     * inferred pipe, so if it depends on something else, add an extra SYNC.nop.
+    * Since Xe-HP the SWSB of an in-order instruction carries an explicit pipe
+    * (or A@n for several pipes), so like brw (baked_ordered_dependency_mode)
+    * only instructions that also take an SBID need the extra SYNC there.
     */
+   const bool explicit_pipe = func->shader->devinfo->verx10 >= 125 && !has_sbid;
+
    if (I->op != JAY_OPCODE_SEND &&
+       !explicit_pipe &&
        wait_pipes &&
        (!single_wait ||
         last_pipe != jay_inferred_sync_pipe(func->shader->devinfo, I))) {
